<title>USA: Philip Morris researcher to aid Fla. suits.</title>
<headline>Philip Morris researcher to aid Fla. suits.</headline>
<dateline>CHARLOTTE, N.C. 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A retired Philip Morris Cos Inc. research chief was ordered to give pre-trial testimony for three tobacco lawsuits pending in south Florida, according to Thursday's Richmond (Virginia) Times-Dispatch.</p>
<p>Dr. Thomas Osdene, of Richmond, Virginia where Philip Morris' largest manufacturing site is also based, must give pre-trial testimony despite his poor health, U.S. District Judge Robert Payne ruled on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The Clerk of U.S. District Court told Reuters on Thursday the judge's order was not yet on file.</p>
